  "id": "Compound::DB01129 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Rabeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor, is shown to bind to Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding likely inhibits the enzymatic activity of these cytochrome P450 enzymes, which are critical for the conversion of arachidonic acid into epoxyeicosanoids. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in the epoxygenase activity of arachidonic acid suggests a potential mechanism by which Rabeprazole may modulate the metabolic pathway of arachidonic acid, potentially affecting the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a strong, biologically plausible link between Rabeprazole and Cyp2c9, supported by the shared functional role of Cyp2c19 and Cyp2d6 in arachidonic acid metabolism. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a direct interaction between Rabeprazole and the enzyme, which is a key component in the metabolic pathway leading to the final product.",
